                                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                        sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                        text="&lt;p>&lt;b>The &amp;quot;Migraine Friendly Workspace&amp;quot; quality label from the Swiss Headache Society is based on three e pillars:&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&lt;b>e&lt;/b>mpowerment: Knowledge transfer and prevention; for example, online seminars or live lectures by SKG members, as well as support for sports programmes and offers for health and well-being.&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&lt;b>e&lt;/b>nvironment: There is a place for retreat that can be closed off and is therefore protected from noise, odours and light. If necessary, workplace counselling is performed, and understanding and flexibility within teams are promoted.&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&lt;b>e&lt;/b>ngagement: Through targeted counselling and solution finding, the basis is created so that migraine sufferers can have a fulfilling career. Flexible working hours, the option of working from home and job rotation also help.&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                        textIsRich="true"/>
